# patches/linux_mainline/series — quilt-style ordered apply list.
# One filename per line (relative to this dir). '#' = comment, blank lines OK.
# Applied by scripts/apply-series.sh via `git am` (run from third_party/linux_mainline).
#
# Since RK3506 pinctrl+clk are already in mainline, entries here are typically
# board/DT/defconfig deltas on top of the SoC support — small and upstream-bound.
# Verified 2026-06-15: applying to a clean v7.0.12 (f53879e2e) OR v7.1 tree and
# building `rockchip/rk3506b-aes.dtb` reproduces the reference dtb BYTE-FOR-BYTE
# (sha 2789c26149c79d0d...; dtc is deterministic, no timestamp). Patch is
# version-agnostic within 7.x. v7.1 boots to interactive shell on the board
# (log boot-sdl-2026-06151312-kernel-7.1.txt).

0001-ARM-dts-rockchip-add-rk3506-SoC-AES-RK3506B-board-DT.patch
0002-ARM-dts-rockchip-rk3506b-aes-enable-SFC-SPI-NAND-MTD-partitions.patch
# SFC sampling delay-line tuning — the root fix for the 80 MHz read ECC errors.
# Ports vendor rockchip_sfc_delay_lines_tuning() into the mainline driver
# (writes SFC_DLL_CTRL0 0x3C / SCLK_SMP_DLL). After 0003, 80 MHz is safe.
0003-spi-rockchip-sfc-add-delay-line-tuning.patch
# Persistent-rootfs bootargs (ubi.mtd=5 root=ubi0:rootfs) — the board-verified
# milestone state; harmless for the initramfs-shell boot variant.
0004-ARM-dts-rk3506b-aes-persistent-rootfs-bootargs.patch
# Raise SFC to 80 MHz + rockchip,max-dll=<0x17F> (vendor value). Depends on 0003;
# without it 80 MHz reintroduces the UBI -EBADMSG ECC errors.
0005-ARM-dts-rk3506b-aes-raise-SFC-to-80MHz.patch
